(window.LADDER_CARDS=window.LADDER_CARDS||{})["6·crypt"]=[{"q":"The boxes are said out loud and the pick is kept. What is the secret?","a":"the pick: which member of each box","w":["the boxes","how many boxes there are","nothing: all of it was said"],"why":"The boxes can be heard by anyone. The secret is the pick, a choosing function (6b4)."},
 {"q":"The boxes are {a, b}, {b, c, d} and {a}. Which set of pairs is a pick?","a":"({a, b}, b), ({b, c, d}, d), ({a}, a)","w":["({a, b}, c), ({b, c, d}, d), ({a}, a)","({a, b}, a), ({b, c, d}, b)","({a, b}, a), ({b, c, d}, a), ({a}, a)"],"why":"Each box is paired with one place, and each place is in its box (6b4)."},
 {"q":"You hold the line x. Which line can you say that is true and leaves a listener with cases?","a":"x ∨ y, for a y of your choosing","w":["x ∧ y, for a true y","x ∨ x","x, in other words"],"why":"From x, write x ∨ y, for any y at all (6a2). Its price is the news of which."},
 {"q":"A free option is added to a line. What is the price of the move?","a":"the news of which: the line no longer says which option is the true one","w":["the truth of the line","nothing at all","the option that was added"],"why":"6a2 named the price. Nothing in the or gets the first line back out without cases."},
 {"q":"A box with one member is said out loud. How much does it hide?","a":"nothing: it leaves a listener one case","w":["as much as any other box","half of the pick","everything, since no option was added"],"why":"A box with one member has the factor 1."},
 {"q":"A line with free options is heard by the one meant to know and by a listener. Why does only the first get to the place?","a":"the first held the pick before the line was said","w":["the first hears the line better","the line says which to whoever it is meant for","the listener holds fewer options"],"why":"The news of which is not sent. It has to be held before the sentence is said."},
 {"q":"The boxes have 2, 4 and 1 members. How many picks fit what a listener heard?","a":"8","w":["7","4","2"],"why":"One factor for each box: 2 · 4 · 1 (6c5)."},
 {"q":"The boxes have 2, 3 and 1 members. One more place goes into the box that has 1. How many picks did that one place add?","a":"6","w":["1","2","12"],"why":"The factor of that box goes from 1 to 2, so the count goes from 6 to 12."},
 {"q":"The rule that picks is said out loud and the boxes are kept. What is a listener short of?","a":"what there is to pick from","w":["how the pick is made","nothing","the rule"],"why":"A rule that picks takes a box in and gives a member out. With no box, it gives no place."},
 {"q":"The rule said out loud is “the member that comes first in the alphabet”. A listener sees the pick g from a kept box. Which of b, f and m could also be in that box?","a":"m only","w":["b and f only","all three","none of them"],"why":"Nothing in the box comes before its pick. The pick does not say that m is there, only that it could be."},
 {"q":"A rule promises a pick from every box, and one of the boxes has no member. How many picks does the collection have?","a":"none","w":["one","as many as the other boxes give","it cannot be counted"],"why":"A box with no member has nothing to pick (6b2), and its factor is 0 (6c5)."},
 {"q":"A check opens when a · n = n, and the visitor says both numbers. Which n opens it to every a?","a":"0","w":["1","no n does","every n does"],"why":"The check leans on x/x written for 1, which is good only for x ≠ 0 (6a5)."},
 {"q":"A check opens when a · n = 5 · n. For an n that is not 0, which a opens it?","a":"5, and no other","w":["any a","0","1"],"why":"Do the same to both sides, dividing by n (5g)."},
 {"q":"A lock leans on a free move. What does the lock take on with it?","a":"the condition of the move: where the condition fails, the lock opens to anyone","w":["nothing: a free move costs nothing","the price of the move, paid once when the lock is made","a second lock"],"why":"The price of a free move comes with whatever is built on top of it."},
 {"q":"The condition of a free move is left off the line of a check. What is it then?","a":"a price still owed, which a listener may collect","w":["a price already paid","no longer a condition","part of the secret"],"why":"A condition written on the line is a price paid (6a6: the cost of free is attention)."},
 {"q":"Two sides share the number k · n. k is kept, and anyone may say n. Which n gives a listener the shared number without k?","a":"0: k · 0 = 0 for every k","w":["1: k · 1 = k","the largest n there is","no n does"],"why":"Different k give different k · n only for n ≠ 0."},
 {"q":"The shared number is k · n. A listener heard n = 4 and learns that the shared number is 28. What does the listener hold now?","a":"k = 7, and with it every later shared number","w":["this one shared number and no more","n, and nothing new","k = 24"],"why":"Divide both sides by 4 (5g)."},
 {"q":"A weakness is found in a way of hiding. What does this step take it as?","a":"a reason to go deeper: to find one more way to hide the information","w":["a reason to give the method up","a sign that nothing can be hidden","something to leave off the line"],"why":"Each fix is one more thing hidden, and each has a price of its own to look for."},
 {"q":"The keeper of a secret makes a pick. What does the keeper need?","a":"one good member: a some","w":["every member to be good: an every","no member at all","the pick of the other side"],"why":"The keeper looks until one good member is in hand (2c)."},
 {"q":"A check lets the visitor make a pick. What does the check need?","a":"to be right for every member the visitor may pick","w":["to be right for one member","to be right for the members the keeper would pick","nothing more"],"why":"One member that breaks it is enough, and the one who picks gets to look for it (2c)."},
 {"q":"From ¬x, the line x ⇒ y is written. What does it promise about y?","a":"nothing: its condition is never met","w":["that y is true","that y is not true","that x will be made true"],"why":"An if made true by a false condition is an empty truth (6a3)."},
 {"q":"A check is made of ifs: for each question, if the visitor answers it, the answer is right. Who passes it with no right answer?","a":"a visitor who answers nothing","w":["a visitor who answers one question right","nobody","a visitor who answers every question wrong"],"why":"Each if has a condition that is not met, so each is true, emptily."},
 {"q":"A check made of ifs is passed by a silent visitor. How is it mended?","a":"write an and where the if was: the visitor answers, and the answer is right","w":["add one more if","ask more questions","write an or where the if was"],"why":"A silent visitor does not pass an and."},
 {"q":"Picks are made by a rule, for boxes without end that are said out loud. What does a listener hold after learning the rule once?","a":"every pick","w":["one pick","nothing","the picks so far, and no later one"],"why":"A rule is short. Its price is the same shortness."},
 {"q":"The choosing axiom says that a choosing function exists. What does it say about its pick from one box?","a":"that the pick is a member of that box, and not which member","w":["which member it is","that it is the least member","nothing, not even that it is a member"],"why":"That is all that can be said of it (6b5, 6b8)."},
 {"q":"Why can two people not share a pick that only the choosing axiom gives them?","a":"the axiom hands the pick to no one: neither can say its member from one box","w":["the axiom gives each of them a different pick","the axiom holds only for finitely many boxes","a listener holds the axiom too"],"why":"Each knows that a pick exists. Neither can say one place from it."},
 {"u":"6·crypt.1.1","q":"The boxes are said out loud and the pick is kept. What does a listener hold, and what does the one meant to know hold besides?","a":"the listener holds the boxes; the other holds the pick as well","w":["both hold the pick","the listener holds the pick; the other holds the boxes","neither holds anything"],"why":"Nothing said was untrue and nothing was in a code. The boxes were said, and no more."},
 {"u":"6·crypt.2.1","q":"What does a free option cost, and who goes without when it is added where a listener can hear?","a":"the news of which; the listener is left without it","w":["the truth of the line; the one who says it","nothing; nobody","the option; the one meant to know"],"why":"A free option hides by saying less (6a2)."},
 {"u":"6·crypt.3.1","q":"Why can the one meant to know not get the pick out of the sentence, and how many cases does a box with one member leave?","a":"the sentence no longer says which; one case","w":["the sentence is untrue; no case","the sentence is in a code; two cases","the sentence says which; one case"],"why":"The one meant to know hears the same or as the listener."},
 {"u":"6·crypt.4.1","q":"The rule is said out loud and the boxes are kept. What does a listener hold, and what is the listener short of?","a":"how every pick is made; the boxes to pick from","w":["the boxes; how the pick is made","every pick; nothing","nothing; everything"],"why":"The listener who holds the choice still needs the boxes."},
 {"u":"6·crypt.5.1","q":"A check opens when a · n = n. Which free move does it lean on, and where does that move stop being free?","a":"x/x written for 1; at 0","w":["x + 0 written for x; at 1","an added option; nowhere","x · 1 written for x; at 0"],"why":"At 0 it is 0/0, which has every answer (6a5, 5e5)."},
 {"u":"6·crypt.6.1","q":"Why is a pick that the keeper makes a some, and a pick that the visitor makes an every?","a":"the keeper needs one good member; the check has to hold for whichever member the visitor brings","w":["the keeper picks once; the visitor picks many times","the keeper picks from one box; the visitor from every box","the keeper may be wrong; the visitor may not"],"why":"A choice you keep asks for one good member. A choice you hand over asks you to be ready for every member."},
 {"u":"6·crypt.7.1","q":"A line is an empty if. Why is it true, what does it promise, and what may a listener wrongly take from it?","a":"its condition is not met; nothing; that its condition is sometimes met","w":["its result is true; its result; nothing","its condition is met; its result; that it is untrue","it has no condition; everything; nothing"],"why":"An empty if promises nothing, and the one who says it comes through all the same (6a3)."},
 {"u":"6·crypt.8.1","q":"What does the choosing axiom say about a pick, and why is that not enough for two people?","a":"that one exists, and not which member it takes; neither can say it, so they cannot both use it","w":["which member it takes; a listener hears it too","that none exists; they have to make one","that a rule picks it; the rule can be learned"],"why":"The axiom hands the pick to no one (6b5)."},
 {"u":"6·crypt.9.1","q":"Among the moves to watch out for in hiding a pick, which does a listener gain from?","a":"the ones that leave an opening: a condition left off, a pick handed over, a rule that can be learned, a check passed emptily","w":["none of them","only the ones that say something untrue","all of them alike"],"why":"The others cost the two sides some trouble and give a listener nothing new."}];
